{"t":"2026-09-12 23:58:28","host":"INDEFFJPAT","user":"JayminPatel(INDEFF)","session":"d424817e-9716-410a-9b68-23b3d857a034","plugin":"0.7.10","cwd":"C:\\Users\\JayminPatel(INDEFF)\\AppData\\Roaming\\Claude\\local-agent-mode-sessions\\6fe128da-f189-4ee5-8469-d8457b88628d\\455e9ca8-b491-4fcc-957d-d48fd6156140\\local_3177bdb5-01a9-49a8-ae22-9d6d0d02395e\\outputs","agent":null,"ev":"stop","mount":"D:\\SearchProject","claim":"Three things, one of which is a real defect.\n\n**The 1823 days is a display bug, not a slow disk.** `format_eta` (`app/ui/presenter.py:457`) divides remaining files by `recent_files_per_minute`, which is measured over a 15-minute window (`RATE_WINDOW_S`, `pipeline.py:174`). One file finished in that window gives 1/900×60 = 0.067 files/min. The line beside it prints that with `:,.0f`, so you see **\"0 files/min\"** — but the ETA maths uses the unrounded 0.067. With a scan total in the hundreds of thousands, 0.067 files/min works out to roughly 1800 days. The two halves of the same line contradict each other: a rate that rounds to zero should print `estimating…`, which is what `format_eta` already does when the rate is exactly `0` — the guard at line 467 is `<= 0` and 0.067 slips past it. There's also no ceiling, so a 15-minute sample is allowed to extrapolate over five years.\n\n**The underlying run does look stalled, though.** 0 (or 1) file in fifteen minutes while `reading cover.jpg [1]` is on screen means OCR is grinding or wedged on that image. That is the thing worth looking at — the ETA is just reporting the stall badly. I can't check it from here: the process, `D:\\Leasha\\Data` and the Qt window aren't reachable from this sandbox, so whether OCR is working or hung needs a look at the log on your side.\n\n**Not a bug:** \"10 documents\" in the headline is this run's counter; \"154 documents\" in the table is the index total. Same for 1,493 chunks vs 9,675 passages. Confusing side by side, but correct.\n\nWant me to draft a fix for the ETA line — a minimum-rate guard plus an \"estimating…\" / \"more than a week\" cap — as a work order?","claim_chars":1649,"changed":[]}
